1. Top‑Level Mission Goal (G1)  
   • The overall mission is to “ensure that all required resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent.”  
   • Since the mission may be executed either as a single‑resource process or by engaging multiple robots in parallel for multiple storages, we split G1 into two branches:  
  – G1.1: Single‑Resource Mission (sequential collection then delivery)  
  – G1.2: Multi‑Resource Mission (parallel collect–deliver tasks)  
   • We use the fallback operator at the top level (FALLBACK(G1.1, G1.2)) to denote that if one branch is inapplicable (or fails) the other is used. The “Relation” column is marked OR because only one branch must succeed.

